# Rank 1880 / CVE-2024-42512 (GHSA-h958-fxgg-g7w3, CWE-208 + CWE-639):
# OPCFoundation/UA-.NETStandard decrypts both the UA TCP secure-channel
# handshake and the user-identity token with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 padding whenever
# the deprecated Basic128Rsa15 security policy is enabled. The policy is
# disabled by default. Two legs meet at the same BCL call:
#
#   handshake:    UaSCUaBinaryChannel.Decrypt (Asymmetric.cs:1208) dispatches
#                 the Basic128Rsa15 case to Rsa_Decrypt(..., RsaUtils.Padding.Pkcs1),
#                 which decrypts each block with rsa.Decrypt(input, rsaPadding)
#                 (Rsa.cs:174) after RsaUtils.GetRSAEncryptionPadding maps the
#                 enum to RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1 (RsaUtils.cs:37).
#   application
#   authentication: UserNameIdentityToken.Decrypt (UserIdentityToken.cs:122)
#                 calls SecurityPolicies.Decrypt, whose Basic128Rsa15 case is
#                 the only literal-argument spelling in the tree
#                 (SecurityPolicies.cs:256,
#                 RsaUtils.Decrypt(..., RsaUtils.Padding.Pkcs1)) and again ends
#                 at rsa.Decrypt(input, rsaPadding) (RsaUtils.cs:313).
#
# .NET's RSA.Decrypt with RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1 throws a distinguishable
# CryptographicException on malformed padding and takes a measurably different
# path than a well-formed block, and the stack surfaces the failure as a
# BadSecurityChecksFailed fault on a fresh channel -- an unauthenticated remote
# attacker can submit repeated crafted ciphertexts and read the oracle
# (CWE-208), recover the handshake or password secrets, and bypass application
# authentication (CWE-639). That is exactly the class the shipped concept
# code.RsaPkcs1v15DecryptErrorOracle (VYQL-CRY-032, CWE-203/385 -- CWE-203 is
# this advisory's CWE-208's parent) exists for.
#
# 3543d0292556691f681e39145e2de4526b90487d ("Added a minimal rogue client
# detection mechanism at the transport level") does not touch the crypto, the
# policy dispatch, or the failure handling: the mitigation is purely additive.
# TcpListenerChannel.ProcessClose marks the remote address when a channel faults
# with BadSecurityChecksFailed or BadTcpMessageTypeInvalid under Basic128Rsa15;
# TcpTransportListener instantiates an ActiveClientTracker only when the server
# offers the policy, blocks an address after three failed validations in ten
# seconds for thirty seconds, and OnAccept refuses blocked addresses before
# creating a channel. The vendor's stated remediation is to stop using
# Basic128Rsa15; the change is a rate limit around an unchanged oracle.
#
# What fires today. Three `--cache off` runs per revision over
# Stack/Opc.Ua.Core/Stack/Tcp (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): 24 findings at the
# parent, 25 at the fixed revision, identical rule histograms (VYQL-NUM-005,
# VYQL-INJ-009, VYQL-CFG-014 only) and zero findings on the RSA path or the
# channel-close path. The +1 on the patched revision is the fixed revision's own new
# method (code.ExternalEntryInput @ TcpTransportListener.cs:133 feeding
# code.LogOutput @ :163), so the patched tree scores higher. `vyql match` on a
# minimal repro of the decrypt dispatch labels nothing: no source, no sink, no
# control. VYQL-CRY-032 has no C# emitter at all -- its only binding is the
# Python frontend's OpenSSL heuristic (rsaPkcs1v15DecryptErrorOracle664 over
# python_review: tokens from pyRsaPkcs1v15DecryptErrorOracle).
#
# Minimal pair, measured with an in-worktree probe binding (reverted before
# this commit; the ENGINE-GAPS entry beside the ledger holds it): a
# function-scoped presenceNode binding on callPath rsa.Decrypt plus selector
# RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1 fires VYQL-CRY-032 on the same-function literal
# form and reports nothing on the identical decrypt whose padding arrives
# through GetRSAEncryptionPadding -- the enum member's value crossing the
# helper boundary produces no fact, and csExprShape collapses a member access
# to the same "ID" shape as a bare variable (csharp.go:610), so no token
# carries the distinction at the BCL call site. The same probe measured zero
# VYQL-CRY-032 over the whole Stack/Opc.Ua.Core tree: the reachable set is one
# file (RsaUtils.cs, the helper side), no corpus call site passes the enum
# literally to a BCL decrypt, and shipping the binding would be a detection
# change with no measurable effect anywhere -- recorded as a gap instead.
#
# Closing that gap still would not separate the revisions: the crypto is
# byte-identical across the fixed revisioned revision, so the binding fires on both. The only new
# signal the fixed revision introduces is the tracker, whose names
# (ActiveClientTracker, MarkAsPotentialProblematic, IsBlocked) are the fixing
# commit's own vocabulary -- the measured family where the change lives in named
# helpers and framework hooks so both revisions score identically (rank 1331,
# with 1514/1535/1540/1556/1557/1593 for the configuration-wiring form), and
# the 1380 counterweight does not apply because the fixed revision leaves no documented API
# call inside the guarded function. The nearest absent-control rule,
# VYQL-AUTH-105, is keyed on password-verification vocabulary its clause set
# does not match, and its check would sit in OnAccept -- a different function
# from the operation being limited, the endpointGuarded attribution-gap family
# (1377/1389/1399/1437). Both directions are therefore rejected deliberately.

test "rank1880: (a) the Basic128Rsa15 policy dispatch decrypts the handshake and the identity token with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 padding, whose failure the stack surfaces as a channel fault"
  lang csharp
  file Stack/Opc.Ua.Core/Stack/Tcp/UaSCBinaryChannel.Asymmetric.cs
  reject VYQL-CRY-032
  reject VYQL-AUTH-105
  code
  ```
  // Composed from UaSCBinaryChannel.Asymmetric.cs (Decrypt dispatch),
  // UaSCBinaryChannel.Rsa.cs (Rsa_Decrypt) and
  // Security/Certificates/RsaUtils.cs (GetRSAEncryptionPadding) at the
  // vulnerable revision.
  using System;
  using System.Security.Cryptography;
  using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;

  namespace Opc.Ua.Bindings
  {
      public static class SecurityPolicies
      {
          public const string Basic128Rsa15 = "http://opcfoundation.org/UA/SecurityPolicy#Basic128Rsa15";
      }

      public static class RsaUtils
      {
          public enum Padding { Pkcs1, OaepSHA1, OaepSHA256 }

          internal static RSAEncryptionPadding GetRSAEncryptionPadding(Padding padding)
          {
              switch (padding)
              {
                  case Padding.Pkcs1: return RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1;
                  case Padding.OaepSHA1: return RSAEncryptionPadding.OaepSHA1;
                  default: return RSAEncryptionPadding.OaepSHA256;
              }
          }
      }

      public class UaSCUaBinaryChannel
      {
          private string SecurityPolicyUri;

          private ArraySegment<byte> Rsa_Decrypt(
              ArraySegment<byte> dataToDecrypt,
              ArraySegment<byte> headerToCopy,
              X509Certificate2 encryptingCertificate,
              RsaUtils.Padding padding)
          {
              using (RSA rsa = encryptingCertificate.GetRSAPrivateKey())
              {
                  RSAEncryptionPadding rsaPadding = RsaUtils.GetRSAEncryptionPadding(padding);
                  byte[] decryptedBuffer = new byte[8192];
                  Array.Copy(headerToCopy.Array, headerToCopy.Offset, decryptedBuffer, 0, headerToCopy.Count);

                  byte[] input = new byte[256];
                  for (int ii = dataToDecrypt.Offset; ii < dataToDecrypt.Offset + dataToDecrypt.Count; ii += 256)
                  {
                      Array.Copy(dataToDecrypt.Array, ii, input, 0, input.Length);
                      byte[] plainText = rsa.Decrypt(input, rsaPadding);
                      Array.Copy(plainText, 0, decryptedBuffer, headerToCopy.Count, plainText.Length);
                  }

                  return new ArraySegment<byte>(decryptedBuffer, 0, headerToCopy.Count + 256);
              }
          }

          protected ArraySegment<byte> Decrypt(
              ArraySegment<byte> dataToDecrypt,
              ArraySegment<byte> headerToCopy,
              X509Certificate2 receiverCertificate)
          {
              switch (SecurityPolicyUri)
              {
                  case SecurityPolicies.Basic128Rsa15:
                  {
                      return Rsa_Decrypt(dataToDecrypt, headerToCopy, receiverCertificate, RsaUtils.Padding.Pkcs1);
                  }

                  default:
                  {
                      return dataToDecrypt;
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1880: (b) the change rate-limits repeat security-validation failures at the transport layer and refuses blocked addresses at accept time"
  lang csharp
  file Stack/Opc.Ua.Core/Stack/Tcp/TcpTransportListener.cs
  reject VYQL-CRY-032
  reject VYQL-AUTH-105
  code
  ```
  // The fix's additions: ProcessClose (TcpListenerChannel.cs) marks the
  // remote address when the faulted channel used Basic128Rsa15, and OnAccept
  // (TcpTransportListener.cs) refuses addresses the tracker has blocked.
  using System;
  using System.Net;
  using System.Net.Sockets;

  namespace Opc.Ua.Bindings
  {
      public class ActiveClientTracker
      {
          public bool IsBlocked(IPAddress ipAddress)
          {
              return false;
          }

          public void AddClientAction(IPAddress ipAddress)
          {
          }
      }

      public class TcpListenerChannel
      {
          private TcpTransportListener m_listener;
          private string SecurityPolicyUri;
          private object Socket;

          public void ProcessClose(uint statusCode, bool close)
          {
              if (close)
              {
                  // mark the RemoteAddress as potential problematic if Basic128Rsa15
                  if ((SecurityPolicyUri == SecurityPolicies.Basic128Rsa15) &&
                      (statusCode == 2147549189 || statusCode == 2147484186))
                  {
                      var tcpTransportListener = m_listener as TcpTransportListener;
                      if (tcpTransportListener != null)
                      {
                          tcpTransportListener.MarkAsPotentialProblematic(
                              ((IPEndPoint)((SocketWrapper)Socket).RemoteEndpoint).Address);
                      }
                  }

                  // close channel immediately.
                  ChannelFaulted();
              }
          }

          private void ChannelFaulted()
          {
          }
      }

      internal class SocketWrapper
      {
          public EndPoint RemoteEndpoint;
      }

      public class TcpTransportListener
      {
          private ActiveClientTracker m_activeClientTracker;
          private object m_channels;
          private object m_lock = new object();

          internal void MarkAsPotentialProblematic(IPAddress remoteEndpoint)
          {
              m_activeClientTracker?.AddClientAction(remoteEndpoint);
          }

          private void OnAccept(object sender, SocketAsyncEventArgs e)
          {
              TcpListenerChannel channel = null;
              bool repeatAccept = false;
              do
              {
                  bool isBlocked = false;

                  // Filter out the Remote IP addresses which are detected with potential problematic behavior
                  if (m_activeClientTracker != null)
                  {
                      IPAddress ipAddress = ((IPEndPoint)e?.AcceptSocket?.RemoteEndPoint)?.Address;
                      if (ipAddress != null && m_activeClientTracker.IsBlocked(ipAddress))
                      {
                          isBlocked = true;
                      }
                  }

                  repeatAccept = false;
                  lock (m_lock)
                  {
                      var channels = m_channels;
                      if (channels != null && !isBlocked)
                      {
                          channel = new TcpListenerChannel();
                      }
                  }
              } while (repeatAccept);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1880: (c) the frontend pair -- a decrypt whose PKCS#1 v1.5 padding is the call's own argument, beside the identical decrypt whose padding arrives through the padding helper"
  lang csharp
  file Stack/Opc.Ua.Core/Security/Certificates/Pair.cs
  reject VYQL-CRY-032
  code
  ```
  // The literal form (first class) is what a C# binding for
  // code.RsaPkcs1v15DecryptErrorOracle can see today and fired under the
  // probe; the helper form (second class) is the real tree's only spelling
  // and reported nothing -- the enum member's value crosses a function
  // boundary that emits no fact. No shipped binding covers either.
  using System.Security.Cryptography;
  using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;

  namespace Opc.Ua.Security.Certificates
  {
      public class LiteralPaddingDecrypt
      {
          public byte[] DecryptHandshake(byte[] input, X509Certificate2 cert)
          {
              using (RSA rsa = cert.GetRSAPrivateKey())
              {
                  return rsa.Decrypt(input, RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1);
              }
          }
      }

      public static class RsaUtils
      {
          public enum Padding { Pkcs1, OaepSHA1, OaepSHA256 }

          internal static RSAEncryptionPadding GetRSAEncryptionPadding(Padding padding)
          {
              switch (padding)
              {
                  case Padding.Pkcs1: return RSAEncryptionPadding.Pkcs1;
                  default: return RSAEncryptionPadding.OaepSHA256;
              }
          }
      }

      public class HelperPaddingDecrypt
      {
          public byte[] DecryptHandshake(byte[] input, X509Certificate2 cert)
          {
              using (RSA rsa = cert.GetRSAPrivateKey())
              {
                  RSAEncryptionPadding rsaPadding = RsaUtils.GetRSAEncryptionPadding(RsaUtils.Padding.Pkcs1);
                  return rsa.Decrypt(input, rsaPadding);
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```
